  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "since the sdk 3.0 update a lot of sdk 3.0 world/instances has been attacked by somthing that cheaters called a nuke. this nuke can break a lot of script on maps and can even crash the instance.\nthat nuke strongly rely on the function SendCustomNetworkEvent(event, (all, master)). the cheater just need to loop every Event on the map and do a SendCustomNetworkEvent on every event on the map to all players, it's absurdly easy to do.\nthe only fix to avoid such nuke to crash our maps is to change EVERY single event string name to add an underscore before it like that \"_MyEvent\"\nthis is a really tough process, because you can forget a lot of thing and maybe break your scripts.\nit would be much better to be able to disallow using the SendCustomNetworkEvent function or just make something to be able to verify who sended it and being able to cancel it",
